  "grammar_explanations": [
    {
      "slug": "imperative: affirmative and negative (Open/Don't run)",
      "title_form": "Imperativo: afirmativo y negativo",
      "title_target": "Imperative: Affirmative and Negative",
      "description_md_form": "El **imperativo** se usa para dar **instrucciones** u **órdenes** directas. Es la forma más simple del verbo: usamos el verbo en su forma base, sin sujeto.\n\n**Afirmativo:** `Open your book.` (Abre tu libro.)\n**Negativo:** `Don't run.` (No corras.)\n\nPara el negativo, ponemos **`Don't`** antes del verbo. Esta forma es igual para todas las personas (you, we, they).\n\n**Estructura:**\n- Afirmativo: `Verbo` + complemento\n- Negativo: `Don't` + verbo + complemento\n\nEjemplos: `Listen to the teacher.` / `Don't stop here.`",
      "description_md_target": "The **imperative** is used to give **instructions** or direct **orders**. It is the simplest verb form: we use the base verb, without a subject.\n\n**Affirmative:** `Open your book.`\n**Negative:** `Don't run.`\n\nFor the negative, put **`Don't`** before the verb. This form is the same for all persons (you, we, they).\n\n**Structure:**\n- Affirmative: `Verb` + complement\n- Negative: `Don't` + verb + complement\n\nExamples: `Listen to the teacher.` / `Don't stop here.`",
      "grammar_structure": "Affirmative: Verb + complement | Negative: Don't + verb + complement",
      "conjugation_table": {
        "name": "imperative",
        "headers": [
          "Forma",
          "Afirmativo",
          "Negativo"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "you (singular)",
            "Open",
            "Don't open"
          ],
          [
            "you (plural)",
            "Open",
            "Don't open"
          ],
          [
            "we",
            "Let's open",
            "Don't open"
          ]
        ]
      },
